<title>INDIA: Indian exports fell 3.8 percent in Nov.</title>
<headline>Indian exports fell 3.8 percent in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-01-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian merchandise exports declined to $2.48 billion in November, down 3.8 percent from $2.58 billion in the same month in 1995, the government said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE   Nov 96    Nov 95</p>
<p>    Exports		  2.48	2.58</p>
<p>    Imports		  2.95	3.10</p>
<p>    Trade balance	 -0.47     -0.52</p>
<p>Note - Figures, in billions of dollars, may not add up due to rounding.  </p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Merchandise exports totalled $21.39 billion in April-November 1996, up 7.81 percent from the same period in 1995, the statement said.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE   Apr-Nov 1996     Apr-Nov 1995</p>
<p>    Exports		     21.39		19.84</p>
<p>    Imports		     24.22		23.14</p>
<p>    Trade balance	     -2.83		-3.30</p>
<p>Note - Figures, in billions of dollars, may not add up due to rounding.</p>
</text>
